0,Gongduk | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/goe/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..7RFLr8CoXB7Z4uaAmQd_qGynn3aY7YsXbqhA3vh2leM,Gongduk is an endangered indigenous language of Bhutan. It belongs to the Sino-Tibetan language family.,Gongduk,Sino-Tibetan
1,Gongduk - goe (Sino-Tibetan) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/goe/,"Gongduk (goe) is part of the Sino-Tibetan family and Sino-Tibetan, Tibeto-Burman, Western Tibeto-Burman, Bodish class. Gongduk speaking People Groups across the world: Fast Facts",Gongduk,Sino-Tibetan
2,About Gongduk language • Mandalas Life,https://mandalas.life/tag/gongduk-language/,"About Gongduk language. Gongduk or Gongdu is an endangered Sino-Tibetan language spoken by about 1,000 people in a few inaccessible villages located near the Kuri Chhu river in the Gongdue Gewog of Mongar District in eastern Bhutan.",Gongduk,Sino-Tibetan
3,Sino-Tibetan Branches Project (STBP) by Andy Hsiu,https://sites.google.com/site/sinotibetanbranches/,"Welcome to Andy Hsiu's Sino-Tibetan Branches Project (STBP) site, an online encyclopedia covering the branches of the Sino-Tibetan language family. Notes on the positions of each branch with Sino-Tibetan are discussed, with a particular emphasis on lexical isoglosses.",Gongduk,Sino-Tibetan
