6,(PDF) Gongduk agreement morphology in functional and diachronic...,https://web.archive.org/web/20210730071335/https://www.academia.edu/38142901/Gongduk_agreement_morphology_in_functional_and_diachronic_perspective,"Gongduk (Trans-Himalayan, Central Bhutan) is, besides Black Mountain Mönpa/Olekha, the only Bhutanese language to exhibit biactantial agreement morphology.",Gongduk,Sino-Tibetan
